INFO  [Claude Code] I've successfully resolved all 5 issues by adding a new factory method to the existing `SettlementGeneratorDiffblueBase` test class. Here's what I did:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Solution Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] All 5 issues had the same root cause: the `SettlementGenerator` class methods (`settlementInfo`, `settlementNPV`, `settlementNPVPrevious`, `settlementNPVNext`, `settlementTimeNext`) were throwing `NullPointerException` because the internal `settlement` field was `null` when these methods were called during testing.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### What I Changed
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I added a new factory method `createSettlementGeneratorWithMinimalSettlement()` to the file:
INFO  [Claude Code] `src/test/java/net/finmath/smartcontract/settlement/SettlementGeneratorDiffblueBase.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This factory method:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Creates a new `SettlementGenerator` instance
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Creates a minimally initialized `Settlement` object (non-null but with no fields set)
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Uses reflection to inject the `Settlement` object into the `SettlementGenerator`'s private `settlement` field
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Returns the configured `SettlementGenerator`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This approach is different from the existing `createSettlementGeneratorWithInitializedSettlement()` factory method, which sets ALL fields. The new factory provides just enough initialization to prevent NPE while allowing the test methods to populate specific fields in isolation.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
